// [fr.LazyAdd] sums as operands, which are only < 2q rather than canonical; the
// relaxed LazyMul contract covers that, at the cost of a slightly wider output:
//
//	t0, t1, t2  canonical operands  → < 9q/8
//	t3, t4, t5  operands < 2q       → < 3q/2
//
// Each coefficient then adds a multiple of q large enough to cover everything
// subtracted from it, so the difference never underflows, and one reduceSparse
// finishes the job:
//
//	c0 = t0+t3 +3q −t1−t2    subtrahend < 2.25q  → in [0, 5.625q)
//	c1 = t4+t3 +4q −t0−2·t1  subtrahend < 3.375q → in [0, 7q)
//	c2 = t5+t1 +2q −t0       subtrahend < 9q/8   → in [0, 4.625q)
